// Money Flow Reversion
//
// The money flow index is RSI weighted by volume: it asks not just whether price rose, but
// whether volume came with it. Below 20 is exhaustion with the sellers spent.
//
// It is the only reversion rule here that can see volume, which is exactly why it belongs
// beside RSI — compare the two on the same instrument and the difference IS the information
// volume adds, measured rather than asserted.
strategy("Money Flow Reversion", overlay = false)

m = mfi(14)

plot(m,  title = "MFI", color = color.accent)
plot(20, title = "Oversold",   color = color.mute, style = style.step)
plot(80, title = "Overbought", color = color.mute, style = style.step)

if crossover(m, 20)
    strategy.entry("mfi", strategy.long)

if crossunder(m, 55)
    strategy.close("mfi")
